WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.180
After years of experience with Manuka honey for skincare,

00:00:03.181 --> 00:00:04.581
this is how I give myself, like,

00:00:04.582 --> 00:00:06.581
new skin. After I've been traveling or,

00:00:06.582 --> 00:00:07.821
you know, when you just had, like,

00:00:07.822 --> 00:00:09.581
a long weekend, you wanna, like,

00:00:09.582 --> 00:00:12.501
literally peel off your layer of skin and place it with a new one.

00:00:12.502 --> 00:00:15.301
I'll first exfoliate. And I have the most dry,

00:00:15.302 --> 00:00:17.421
sensitive skin that if I exfoliate,

00:00:17.422 --> 00:00:19.341
I need something hydrating,

00:00:19.342 --> 00:00:19.701
healing,

00:00:19.702 --> 00:00:23.301
and barrier repairing on my skin that isn't gonna clog my pores.

00:00:23.302 --> 00:00:27.061
And nothing's ever done that for me more than just manuka honey,

00:00:27.062 --> 00:00:29.381
antifungal, antibacterial,

00:00:29.382 --> 00:00:31.821
anti inflammatory, any inflammation,

00:00:31.822 --> 00:00:33.861
irritation is just going to calm down.

00:00:33.862 --> 00:00:37.541
And that's so important because irritation leads to inflammation,

00:00:37.542 --> 00:00:38.861
that leads to breakout,

00:00:38.862 --> 00:00:41.461
which is why I used to breakout after exfoliating.

00:00:41.462 --> 00:00:44.781
Not anymore. I let that sit for pretty much as long as I can tolerate

00:00:44.782 --> 00:00:45.941
because it starts dripping.

00:00:45.942 --> 00:00:48.261
I run some warm water, clean towels,

00:00:48.262 --> 00:00:50.221
soak this or a cloth in warm water,

00:00:50.222 --> 00:00:52.061
wipe it off right after the sink,

00:00:52.062 --> 00:00:54.621
I have some manuka honey, some water on my face,

00:00:54.622 --> 00:00:56.101
gonna rub them in together.

00:00:56.102 --> 00:00:58.981
If this on as a way longer face mask for, like,

00:00:58.982 --> 00:01:02.061
a few hours. If you're going outside doing work or sweating,

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:05.341
I don't recommend. I'm literally gonna be in a cool room working.

00:01:05.342 --> 00:01:06.901
Yeah, it'll feel like brand new,

00:01:06.902 --> 00:01:09.018
fresh skin. As always. Let me know if you try.
